# Motion Streaming Investigation

Attempted:

```bash
rpicam-vid -t 0 --inline --listen -o tcp://0.0.0.0:8888
```

Encountered:

```text
failed to bind listen socket
```

Resolution:

```bash
pkill -f rpicam-vid
```

Retested using a different port:

```bash
rpicam-vid -t 0 --inline --listen -o tcp://0.0.0.0:9999
```

Eventually abandoned in favour of OpenCV motion detection.

---

# Motion Package Investigation

Installed:

```bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install motion -y
```

Verified:

```bash
motion -h
```

Installed compatibility tools:

```bash
sudo apt install v4l-utils -y
```

Camera visible via:

```bash
v4l2-ctl --list-devices
```

Motion failed under Bookworm:

```text
VIDIOC_STREAMON: Invalid argument
```

Decision:

```text
Abandon Motion.
Use Picamera2 + OpenCV instead.
```

